---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About the Bitcoin Crimes archive: purpose, audience, and independence."
>
  <div class="container-narrow pt-10 sm:pt-14 pb-16 prose-case">
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl mb-4">About</h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-8">
      Bitcoin Crimes is an independent research archive. It tracks high-profile
      criminal cases where Bitcoin was central, and places them in historical
      context with citations you can check.
    </p>

    <h2>Why this exists</h2>
    <p>
      Public discussion of “crypto crime” often mixes rumor, undated dollar
      figures, and guilt-by-association. This project prefers fewer cases, fully
      sourced, over a firehose of weak claims.
    </p>

    <h2>Audience</h2>
    <p>
      Journalists, researchers, educators, and curious readers who want a
      careful starting point — not a substitute for reading the court file.
    </p>

    <h2>Independence</h2>
    <p>
      No affiliation with any government agency, exchange, or law firm. Content
      is editorial and may be incomplete. See the
      <a href="/methodology">methodology</a> for inclusion rules.
    </p>

    <h2>Contributing</h2>
    <p>
      Improvements are welcome when they improve accuracy: primary source links,
      corrections to dates or amounts, clearer legal-status labels. Unsourced
      accusations will be rejected.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
